#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:560
msgid "Counting is so common that the module `collections` (it comes with Python) has a dictionary made for it: **`Counter`**. Give it the values, and it counts them:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:575
msgid "A `Counter` is a dictionary: `items()`, `sorted(...)` and `dict(counts)` work as in [session 6](./06-dictionaries.md#_3-iterating-over-a-dictionary). Two differences: a missing key gives `0` instead of a `KeyError`, and `most_common(n)` gives the `n` largest counts, largest first."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:580
msgid "On the portfolio - the loans per product, from a generator expression ([session 5](./05-lists-advanced.md#_3-generator-expressions-no-list-in-memory)), without a list in memory:"
