#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:594
msgid "You can also start with an empty `Counter()` and add one value at a time - useful in a loop that does more than counting. `+= 1` works for a new key too, because the missing key starts at `0`. Two counters are equal (`==`) when they have the same values with the same counts:"
