#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1777
msgid "A `?` after the quantifier makes it **lazy**: as little as possible."
msgstr ""

#. box title
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1787
msgid "`.*` takes too much"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1788
msgid "`.*` is the most common cause of a wrong match: it runs to the end of the line, then steps back. When the text between two markers cannot contain the marker, write a class with `^`: `\"[^\"]*\"`, `\\([^)]*\\)`."
